name: browser-rp-contract
description: Preserve the shared Browser RP credential, refresh, cookie, and authority/RP separation contract.
---

# Browser RP Contract

- Authority controllers and self-RP controllers have separate bases. A parent Browser Session may
  authorize an explicitly bound OIDC request, but it is never an RP credential fallback.
- Warp, Edit and Core application surfaces use the shared Browser RP lifecycle. Do not reintroduce
  generic root authentication into an RP controller or RP credential lifecycle into an Authority
  controller. Do not add old Side or `core-next-rp` aliases.
- Refresh evaluates refresh credentials independently of access credentials. GET/HEAD orchestration
  and unsafe-request orchestration remain separate; unsafe requests complete CSRF, Origin and Fetch
  Metadata checks before refresh and mutation.
- Credential failure and dependency failure have distinct observable outcomes. A credential failure
  clears invalid RP cookies; a dependency failure preserves them and returns an explicit failure.
  No silent refresh, fallback cookie, retry or grace protocol is permitted.
- Logout clears the originating RP's own browser state before it redirects to the OP; the OP then
  commits the authority stop (D-188). Sibling RPs learn of it through back-channel logout, never
  synchronously.
  Browser history clearing uses official Inertia primitives only and never stores one-time secrets in
  page history.
